            <div xml:id="d561">

                <pb facs="0686" n="566" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg566"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00 Revolutions/44: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Lay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-04-28T17:00:00-06:00">April 28, 1931—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 29—11:05 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>79. Department’s telegram No. 30, April 27, 7 p.m. Instructions regarding Naval
                    Attachè strictly complied with and views concerning <pb facs="0687" n="567"
                        xml:id="pg567"/> company’s planes respected. President now considering
                    purchasing an unused plane here belonging to United Fruit Company and manning it
                    with Honduran forces for observation purposes.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
